# Caddy for Open Dots. With a real domain Caddy gets and renews the certificate by itself.
#
# What the server relies on, and this file provides (Caddy does the first three by default):
#   - X-Forwarded-For is set to the connecting address: Caddy does not believe a header the client
#     sent, so a client cannot choose which address its failed sign-ins are counted against.
#   - X-Forwarded-Proto says the visit was HTTPS, so the sign-in cookie is marked Secure.
#   - Host is passed through unchanged (the server answers only to names it knows).
#   - The event stream is not buffered (flush_interval -1).
#   - Uploads up to the server's own 10 MB image limit (plus form overhead) pass.
#   - /hooks/ goes to the app like everything else: webhooks carry their own per-routine secret.
# OPEN_DOTS_CADDY_TLS is empty for automatic HTTPS, or `tls internal` for a private name or a test.
{$OPEN_DOTS_DOMAIN} {
	{$OPEN_DOTS_CADDY_TLS}

	request_body {
		max_size 20MB
	}

	reverse_proxy open-dots:8000 {
		flush_interval -1
	}
}
